---
// src/pages/surveys/wy-voter-access/info/index.astro
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Wyoming Voter Access | Grassroots Movement" description="Background and source notes for the Wyoming Voter Access Survey.">
  <main>
    <h1>Wyoming Voter Access</h1>
    <p>
      Voting should be simple, secure, and open to every eligible citizen.
    </p>
    <p>
      Wyoming already has a local election system run by county clerks, election workers, and community volunteers. The goal is to build on that system.
    </p>
    <p>
      This survey focuses on three simple ideas:
    </p>

    <h2>1. Give people time to vote.</h2>
    <p>
      Create a statewide voting holiday for the primary and general election, or expand voting time access so working people have a fair chance to cast a ballot.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Make registration easier.</h2>
    <p>
      Automatically register eligible Wyoming residents when getting or renewing a Wyoming driver's license or state ID.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Protect same-day registration.</h2>
    <p>
      Keep the ability for eligible citizens to register and vote on Election Day.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Optional all-candidate primary ballot.</h2>
    <p>
      The optional all-candidate primary ballot question asks whether Wyoming should offer voters another ballot choice in addition to existing party primary ballots. This optional ballot would list all candidates for each office and allow one choice per office regardless of party affiliation. The question measures public preference on primary ballot access. It does not remove voter eligibility checks, county clerk verification, or existing election security rules.
    </p>

    <p>
      The principle is simple: keep elections secure, verify eligibility, and make voting as easy as possible for every eligible Wyoming citizen.
    </p>

    <h2>Fact notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The 2026 Wyoming primary election is August 18, 2026.</li>
      <li>The 2026 Wyoming general election is November 3, 2026.</li>
      <li>Wyoming's 2026 Secretary of State election calendar says voters may register and vote at polling places on Election Day.</li>
      <li>Wyoming law currently provides one hour of paid voting leave in certain circumstances under W.S. 22-2-111.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Source notes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://sos.wyo.gov/Elections/Docs/2026/2026_Key_Election_Dates.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Wyoming Secretary of State 2026 Key Election Dates
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://wyoleg.gov/statutes/compress/title22.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          Wyoming Statute 22-2-111, Employees time off to vote
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Facebook share text</h2>
    <p>
      Wyoming voices matter.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm asking voters to take a short survey about voter access in Wyoming.
    </p>
    <p>
      Should Wyoming create a statewide voting holiday?<br />
      Should eligible residents be automatically registered to vote when getting or renewing a driver's license or state ID?<br />
      Should Wyoming protect same-day voter registration?<br />
      Should Wyoming offer voters an optional all-candidate primary ballot?
    </p>
    <p>
      Take the short survey and share it with Wyoming friends:
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/surveys/wy-voter-access">/surveys/wy-voter-access</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Want to know more?
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/surveys/wy-voter-access/info">/surveys/wy-voter-access/info</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Exact questions and results will be published in aggregate.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a class="button button--primary" href="/surveys/wy-voter-access">Take the survey</a>
      <a class="button button--secondary" href="/surveys/list/">Back to surveys</a>
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
